ao_audiotrack: round the buffer size to whole frames, not samples

AudioTrack throws "Invalid audio buffer size" unless the size is a multiple
of the frame size (bytes per sample * channels). mpv rounds min/max only to
bytes per sample, so when the driver minimum is large enough that the
150 ms cap is chosen, some rates break: 22050 Hz stereo float gives 26460
bytes (3307.5 frames) and the AO fails, leaving playback without sound.
Round to the frame instead. Frames are not always a power of two (3, 5, 6
or 7 channels), so MP_ALIGN_UP cannot be used.

Issue: https://github.com/midasvo/ephyra/issues/659
Upstream: not fixed in mpv v0.42.0 or master (checked 2026-11-23); worth
sending to mpv. Drop this patch once an mpv release contains a fix.

diff --git a/audio/out/ao_audiotrack.c b/audio/out/ao_audiotrack.c
index f483ccc..f9dddf7 100644
--- a/audio/out/ao_audiotrack.c
+++ b/audio/out/ao_audiotrack.c
@@ -738,11 +738,14 @@ static int init(struct ao *ao)
 
     // Choose double of the minimum buffer size suggested by the driver, but not
     // less than 75ms or more than 150ms.
+    // AudioTrack rejects sizes that are not whole frames. A frame is not always
+    // a power of two (e.g. 5.1), so MP_ALIGN_UP can't be used to round to it.
     const int bps = af_fmt_to_bytes(ao->format);
-    int min = 0.075 * p->samplerate * bps * ao->channels.num;
+    const int frame = bps * ao->channels.num;
+    int min = 0.075 * p->samplerate * frame;
     int max = min * 2;
-    min = MP_ALIGN_UP(min, bps);
-    max = MP_ALIGN_UP(max, bps);
+    min = (min + frame - 1) / frame * frame;
+    max = (max + frame - 1) / frame * frame;
     p->size = MPCLAMP(buffer_size * 2, min, max);
     MP_VERBOSE(ao, "Setting bufferSize = %d (driver=%d, min=%d, max=%d)\n", p->size, buffer_size, min, max);
     mp_assert(p->size % bps == 0);
